```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .joke-container {
            border: 2px solid blue;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
            background-color: white;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        h1 {
            color: blue;
        }
        button {
            background-color: yellow;
            color: black;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: orange;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="joke-container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <p id="joke">[Funny Joke]</p>
        <button onclick="revealPunchline()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealPunchline() {
            const jokeElement = document.getElementById('joke');
            jokeElement.textContent = "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!";
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple webpage with a joke container that initially displays "[Funny Joke]" and a button labeled "Push to reveal punchline". When the button is clicked, it reveals a real joke about atoms. You can replace the joke text with any other joke you like!
